WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.480
A banknote is a small
piece of paper and ink.

2
00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:06.120
On its own, it's worth almost nothing.

3
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.820
Yet hand one over in a shop,

4
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.090
and you walk out with
real food or new shoes.

5
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:14.730
Stranger still: in 2014,
the Bank of England put

6
00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:18.530
notes and coins at only
about 3 per cent of money.

7
00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:20.950
So why will a shop hand over real goods

8
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.860
for a piece of paper that is worth almost

9
00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.640
nothing on its own?

10
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:28.300
In this mission, you'll uncover
what money really does for us,

11
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.960
every day. Then you'll
follow savings into a bank,

12
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.730
and out again as a loan to a business.

13
00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:39.000
Your mission: explain why a piece
of paper can buy real goods.
